---
slug: captcha-verify
method: post
---
{% comment %}
  Example-app POST handler for the captcha demo (NOT part of the distributed module).
  Picks the matching provider secret. Turnstile / hCaptcha / reCAPTCHA v2 use public TEST secrets
  (always pass); reCAPTCHA v3 reads a real secret from CAPTCHA_RECAPTCHA_V3_SECRET. A real
  integration always reads secrets from constants, e.g. context.constants.CAPTCHA_TURNSTILE_SECRET.

  SECURITY (demo only): this picks the provider — and therefore the secret — from a
  client-submitted field (context.params.provider, set by a hidden input in captcha-demo.liquid).
  That is safe HERE only because every branch uses an always-pass TEST secret. DO NOT copy this
  shape into production: an attacker who controls `provider` could steer verification to a weaker
  or test path and bypass the captcha. In real code, fix the provider server-side and read its
  secret from a constant — never branch on client input to choose the secret:

    function result = 'modules/captchas/commands/captcha/verify',
      provider: 'turnstile',
      secret: context.constants.CAPTCHA_TURNSTILE_SECRET
{% endcomment %}
{% liquid
  assign provider = context.params.provider | default: 'turnstile'
  case provider
    when 'hcaptcha'
      assign secret = '0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000'
      # hCaptcha secrets are account-wide, so bind the token to this form's sitekey.
      # Always pass expected_sitekey when the account has more than one hCaptcha sitekey.
      assign expected_sitekey = '10000000-ffff-ffff-ffff-000000000001'
    when 'recaptcha'
      assign secret = '6LeIxAcTAAAAAGG-vFI1TnRWxMZNFuojJ4WifJWe'
    when 'recaptcha_v3'
      assign secret = context.constants.CAPTCHA_RECAPTCHA_V3_SECRET
    else
      assign provider = 'turnstile'
      assign secret = '1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA'
  endcase

  if provider == 'recaptcha_v3'
    function result = 'modules/captchas/commands/captcha/verify', provider: provider, secret: secret, min_score: 0.5, expected_action: 'demo_submit'
  else
    # expected_sitekey is only set for hCaptcha; it is nil for the others, which ignore it
    function result = 'modules/captchas/commands/captcha/verify', provider: provider, secret: secret, expected_sitekey: expected_sitekey
  endif
%}
{% if result.valid %}
  <h1>✅ Captcha passed ({{ provider }})</h1>
  <p>Submitted message: {{ context.params.message }}</p>
{% else %}
  <h1>❌ Captcha failed ({{ provider }})</h1>
  <ul>
    {% for error in result.errors %}
      {% for key in error[1] %}
        <li>{{ key | t }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endif %}

{% if result.score != blank %}
  <p>reCAPTCHA v3 score: <strong>{{ result.score }}</strong> (action: {{ result.action }})</p>
{% endif %}

<p><a href="/captcha-demo?provider={{ provider }}">← Back to the form</a></p>

{% if result.response %}
  <h2>Raw provider response</h2>
  <pre>{{ result.response | json }}</pre>
{% endif %}
